  "step_3": "The decision reason requires comparing the least probable outcomes (i.e., the outcomes with the lowest probability) and preferring the one with the more favorable (less severe) outcome. In this case, the least probable outcome in B is -6000 Euros at 0.1%, and in A it is -3000 Euros at 0.2%. The reason would prefer A because -3000 is more favorable than -6000, even though it occurs at a higher probability. However, the individual’s justification focuses solely on the magnitude of the loss being 'wesentlich geringer' in A, without referencing the probability of the least probable outcome or comparing the favorable nature of the least probable outcomes. The individual does not mention the 0.1% vs. 0.2% probabilities or the concept of 'least probable outcomes' as defined in the reason. Thus, while the individual ends up choosing A, the reasoning is based on loss magnitude rather than the structured comparison of the least probable outcomes as required by the decision reason. Therefore, the decision reason was not explicitly or appropriately used in the deliberation process.",
